1
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:38,250
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,410 --> 00:01:40,960
[Episode 14]

3
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:45,280
Actually, his birthday is coming up soon.

4
00:01:45,509 --> 00:01:47,440
You two can celebrate it together.

5
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:49,920
Many things can be cleared up
face to face.

6
00:01:51,229 --> 00:01:52,400
He hasn't celebrated his birthday

7
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,759
with me for many years.

8
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,350
Well,

9
00:01:58,039 --> 00:01:59,840
celebrate it with him this year.

10
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:20,430
[Jiangcheng Same-City, Short-Term Rentals]

11
00:02:20,460 --> 00:02:20,880
[Fully Furnished Single-Story
Courtyard House in Waimao]

12
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:21,350
[Move-in Ready: RMB 400/Day,
Monthly Rent Negotiable]

13
00:02:37,610 --> 00:02:39,590
[Discover Life]

14
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:41,400
[Description of the House]

15
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,120
Come on.

16
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:04,520
Here.

17
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:08,960
Nice shot!

18
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:09,870
-Come on.
-Nice!

19
00:03:09,870 --> 00:03:10,930
Let's call it a day.

20
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:12,110
Get some rest.

21
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:19,090
Let's take a break.

22
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:29,079
Don't mention the warm-up match
these days.

23
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:30,030
-Got it.
-Got it.

24
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:32,630
They are from a professional team
after all.

25
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:34,030
It's normal to lose, huh?

26
00:03:34,190 --> 00:03:35,280
Are you stupid?

27
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,030
When has our captain
ever scored in single digits

28
00:03:37,030 --> 00:03:38,560
and had double-digit turnovers?

29
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,620
He is usually so strict with himself.

30
00:03:42,079 --> 00:03:44,120
He celebrates his birthday
with us every year.

31
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:48,050
When I asked him yesterday,
he actually said he wouldn't celebrate it.

32
00:03:53,630 --> 00:03:55,000
Stand up! Stand up now!

33
00:03:58,310 --> 00:03:59,000
Captain!

34
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,960
Happy birthday!

35
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:06,800
Thank you.

36
00:04:07,910 --> 00:04:09,470
Captain, relax a bit.

37
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:10,730
Let's go out together.

38
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,280
-Yeah!
-That's right.

39
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:12,870
No.

40
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:15,240
My mom wants to have dinner
with me tonight.

41
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,070
After that,

42
00:04:16,070 --> 00:04:18,329
I have to review the warm-up match video.

43
00:04:19,510 --> 00:04:21,170
Are you sure you're not going?

44
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:24,560
Alright. Happy birthday.

45
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:27,120
Happy birthday.

46
00:04:27,190 --> 00:04:28,190
Happy birthday, Captain.

47
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:29,950
Happy birthday, Captain.

48
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:32,020
Happy birthday, Captain.

49
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,260
Happy birthday, Captain.

50
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:16,750
[Jiangcheng University Basketball Team]

51
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:18,000
Today is your birthday.

52
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:18,620
[Mom]

53
00:05:18,430 --> 00:05:19,690
Happy birthday to you.

54
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:22,200
Just come over for dinner tonight.

55
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:20,660
[Government Staff Residential Compound]
[Back to the Current Location]

56
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:12,190
[Sweet Day] [Happy Birthday]

57
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:13,870
Han.

58
00:07:14,430 --> 00:07:15,240
You're here.

59
00:07:16,390 --> 00:07:17,990
Didn't we book a restaurant?

60
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:18,900
Why are we here?

61
00:07:19,270 --> 00:07:21,430
Happy birthday, son.

62
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:25,870
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

63
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:29,600
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

64
00:07:29,630 --> 00:07:33,510
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

65
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:37,430
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

66
00:07:38,870 --> 00:07:40,720
Happy birthday!

67
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:43,270
Thank you.

68
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:46,240
Happy birthday,

69
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,680
Xiaoli.

70
00:07:58,159 --> 00:08:00,390
Xiangxiang planned all of this.

71
00:08:01,390 --> 00:08:03,120
Xiangxiang said
when you were in the compound,

72
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,560
you had a great time every year
on your birthday,

73
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,070
so she specially
searched for a place online

74
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:08,920
that looked quite like the compound
in your hometown.

75
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:11,160
And she has even invited some
of your childhood friends in Jiangcheng.

76
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:13,360
Well, she wanted to give you a surprise.

77
00:08:17,420 --> 00:08:18,380
And you, too.

78
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:21,270
You've known Xiangxiang
at school for so long.

79
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:23,250
How could you not realize she was

80
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,510
that little girl from next door?

81
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,360
Make a wish.

82
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:46,090
Xiangxiang.

83
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:50,100
I hope from now on,
you can be full of joy every day

84
00:08:50,910 --> 00:08:52,240
and stay happy forever.

85
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,960
I remember when we were in Grade Three

86
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,200
and had a bicycle race,

87
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,600
we rode all the way from the school gate

88
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,390
to the intersection
in front of our compound's gate.

89
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,320
It seemed only Xiaoli rode slowly.

90
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,720
He was actually riding steadily,

91
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,790
unlike Fatty,

92
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,030
who rode the fastest

93
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:24,890
and ended up crashing into a tree.

94
00:09:26,510 --> 00:09:28,760
I still remember how miserable he looked.

95
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:31,220
Can't you
remember something good about me?

96
00:09:35,870 --> 00:09:36,820
We've been chatting for so long.
Let's have some cake.

97
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:37,510
Well, you...

98
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:38,030
Let's eat.

99
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:39,490
Did you sign the contract?

100
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:46,210
Check the other party's information.

101
00:09:48,550 --> 00:09:50,010
Let's talk about it later.

102
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,270
Thank you.

103
00:09:56,870 --> 00:09:57,480
Mom.

104
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,390
If you're happy, I'm happy.

105
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,320
Does your leg

106
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:09,910
still hurt?

107
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:12,960
It's fine. It'll be better in a while.

108
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,500
You have to be careful.

109
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:27,750
Thank you

110
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:31,240
for being willing to
celebrate your birthday with me.

111
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,620
Thinking about it carefully,

112
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,910
I feel I've let you down.

113
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:45,510
In Kunzhou,
I was always busy with business.

114
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:48,280
When we came to Jiangcheng,

115
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,240
I was busy arguing with your dad.

116
00:10:53,510 --> 00:10:56,040
I didn't pay much attention
to your feelings.

117
00:10:59,270 --> 00:11:00,400
It's all in the past.

118
00:11:00,790 --> 00:11:01,590
It's fine now.

119
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:09,910
I know you love playing basketball,

120
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,240
but I still think it can only be a hobby,

121
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:15,000
not a career.

122
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,510
I'm afraid you'll get hurt.

123
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:20,710
I'm afraid you'll...

124
00:11:23,670 --> 00:11:24,510
I know

125
00:11:25,030 --> 00:11:26,960
you don't like hearing me say this.

126
00:11:27,670 --> 00:11:29,730
Alright. I'll stop talking about it.

127
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,600
Enjoy yourself on your birthday,

128
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,330
and have fun with your friends.

129
00:11:37,790 --> 00:11:39,190
I still have things to do.

130
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,270
Have fun, guys.

131
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:42,630
Goodbye, Mrs. Gu.

132
00:11:42,650 --> 00:11:43,380
Goodbye.

133
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:45,710
[Sweet Day]

134
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:47,920
[Happy Birthday]

135
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,840
Oh, by the way, Xiaoli...

136
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:57,790
I've watched the video

137
00:11:57,790 --> 00:12:00,050
of your last match against that pro team.

138
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,670
Why did you play so badly?

139
00:12:01,670 --> 00:12:02,840
Exactly.

140
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:05,150
Aren't you the ace
of Jiangcheng University?

141
00:12:05,150 --> 00:12:06,630
And the scoring champion or something?

142
00:12:06,630 --> 00:12:08,200
Why did you only score a few points

143
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,060
and keep getting the ball stolen?

144
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,900
I didn't play well.

145
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,460
So even the ace
doesn't play well sometimes?

146
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,200
Even the ace can't play well
every single time.

147
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,000
Who said that?

148
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:20,600
The ace must be perfect.

149
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,720
In every match, regardless of
the strength of the opponent,

150
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:26,180
the ace must maintain stable performances.

151
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:28,480
The ace can't get sick, get hurt,

152
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:30,440
be tired or suffer.

153
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,630
Nor can he...

154
00:12:31,630 --> 00:12:32,510
Nor can he...

155
00:12:32,510 --> 00:12:34,910
Want to go to the toilet
halfway through it.

156
00:12:39,910 --> 00:12:40,870
Do you guys still remember

157
00:12:40,870 --> 00:12:42,870
the game we played when we were kids?

158
00:12:58,510 --> 00:13:00,250
Endless drinking parties!

159
00:13:01,910 --> 00:13:03,770
I have to work overtime every day!

160
00:13:05,460 --> 00:13:07,600
I don't have to write papers anymore!

161
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,150
You're not good at this.

162
00:13:30,150 --> 00:13:31,790
You were already bad at this game
when you were a kid.

163
00:13:31,790 --> 00:13:32,520
Start again.

164
00:13:33,670 --> 00:13:34,480
MVP!

165
00:13:34,910 --> 00:13:35,870
MVP!

166
00:13:35,960 --> 00:13:36,910
MVP!

167
00:13:36,910 --> 00:13:37,840
MVP!

168
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:38,790
MVP!

169
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:39,670
MVP!

170
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:40,560
MVP!

171
00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:41,570
MVP!

172
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:05,480
Thank you.

173
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:11,340
Didn't you also always celebrate
my birthday for me when we were kids?

174
00:14:11,750 --> 00:14:13,000
But back then,

175
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,670
we were too young.

176
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,480
We can't remember many things clearly,

177
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,150
right?

178
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:20,210
Xiangxiang.

179
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:27,970
Actually, I've wanted to tell you who I am
for a long time,

180
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,850
but I just never had the chance.

181
00:14:32,030 --> 00:14:33,390
Later, Fatty told me

182
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:36,570
that you had an accident
while hosting that day.

183
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,600
Originally, I should have been in charge

184
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,200
of those backstage devices.

185
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:43,600
What's more, I also promised you

186
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,060
that I would stay with you.

187
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:46,910
I'm sorry.

188
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,390
Why are you so serious?

189
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,240
That all happened when we were kids.

190
00:14:55,870 --> 00:14:57,130
I know everything now.

191
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:02,480
What's more, I'm already a host
at the campus TV station now,

192
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,460
and it's all thanks to you.

193
00:15:19,030 --> 00:15:20,230
Do you still remember

194
00:15:20,390 --> 00:15:21,600
during the Dragon Boat Festival,

195
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,660
we played Truth or Dare in your house?

196
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:25,600
Yes, I remember.

197
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,440
There's no lie detector now.

198
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,360
But I still want to ask you again.

199
00:15:41,870 --> 00:15:42,510
Is there a girl

200
00:15:42,510 --> 00:15:44,770
you've liked very much since childhood?

201
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:07,910
It's Li Jing
from the building next door, right?

202
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:10,710
I saw you carrying her backpack for her
many times.

203
00:16:11,030 --> 00:16:11,630
No.

204
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,480
Then it must be...

205
00:16:15,870 --> 00:16:17,130
Hua from our compound.

206
00:16:17,790 --> 00:16:19,990
Didn't she always come to play with you?

207
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:21,530
What are you thinking?

208
00:16:30,270 --> 00:16:31,200
Who is it then?

209
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:50,330
Good night.

210
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,030
You look great.

211
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,770
Did your mom pump you up?

212
00:17:17,109 --> 00:17:17,930
Yes, she did.

213
00:17:18,569 --> 00:17:20,210
I don't think it was your mom.

214
00:17:24,270 --> 00:17:25,160
Seriously,

215
00:17:25,589 --> 00:17:27,589
Le Xiaotao gave me some important intel.

216
00:17:27,589 --> 00:17:28,790
Do you want to hear it?

217
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:29,880
Tell me.

218
00:17:30,310 --> 00:17:31,840
In a few days,
Zhou Xiangxiang will participate in

219
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:34,440
the intern streamer audition
for the Starry Sky's basketball program.

220
00:17:34,440 --> 00:17:35,370
Do you know that?

221
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,960
Do you two seldom communicate?

222
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:40,420
Do you want to go together?

223
00:17:46,750 --> 00:17:48,830
Alright. Don't blame me
for not reminding you.

224
00:17:48,830 --> 00:17:50,160
She's auditioning
for a basketball program,

225
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:51,960
which is your area of expertise.

226
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:54,160
You have to take action when it's time.

227
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:07,340
How is it? Are you ready?

228
00:18:09,790 --> 00:18:11,270
Fortunately, my roommates

229
00:18:11,270 --> 00:18:13,200
and those guys from the basketball team

230
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,200
helped me study.

231
00:18:15,070 --> 00:18:17,280
I think it should be fine this time.

232
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,440
You don't need to be too nervous.

233
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,400
With your level,

234
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:21,840
I'm sure you can pass it.

235
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,550
What's more, even if you fail,

236
00:18:23,550 --> 00:18:25,160
it's no big deal, right?

237
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,310
I know.

238
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:30,000
After all, there's the Senior from
the Broadcasting and Hosting Department.

239
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,600
As long as I've tried,
I won't have any regrets.

240
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:41,830
Begin!

241
00:18:45,550 --> 00:18:47,010
-Come on.
-I'll ask first.

242
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:48,110
Which active NBA player

243
00:18:48,110 --> 00:18:50,480
is known for his cute and adorable

244
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,110
nickname?

245
00:18:53,350 --> 00:18:54,590
"Big Baby" Davis.

246
00:18:55,550 --> 00:18:56,640
The "Big Baby" you mentioned

247
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:58,440
has been retired for many years.

248
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,810
It's "Elementary School Student" Curry.

249
00:19:01,030 --> 00:19:01,640
Is that so?

250
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:04,240
Next question.

251
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:06,220
When a player dribbles at a high speed,

252
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:08,790
his body moves in the direction
towards the ipsilateral foot,

253
00:19:08,790 --> 00:19:09,550
and the other foot

254
00:19:09,550 --> 00:19:11,750
moves in the opposite direction
from the foot that landed previously.

255
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:13,920
What is this big-stride
change-of-direction movement called?

256
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:14,920
I know the answer!

257
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:17,240
Crossover, right?

258
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,460
It's called the Euro step. Thank you.

259
00:19:21,110 --> 00:19:21,720
Your turn!

260
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,460
The legends of the Pistons,

261
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:25,430
Ben Wallace and Rasheed Wallace,

262
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:26,790
are known as the Wallaces.

263
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,450
Which of them is the elder one?

264
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:29,350
Ben.

265
00:19:29,550 --> 00:19:30,510
No, no, no.

266
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:31,650
I think it's Rasheed.

267
00:19:31,650 --> 00:19:32,980
His name sounds better.

268
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,030
Among these two people,

269
00:19:35,030 --> 00:19:36,750
one is a white man,
and the other is a black man.

270
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:38,610
They just have the same last name.

271
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:43,310
This is too hard.

272
00:19:48,510 --> 00:19:49,710
There is another way.

273
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,070
Ask Gu Han for help.

274
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:55,500
It's a good way.

275
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,030
I don't think that's a good idea.

276
00:19:59,030 --> 00:20:00,030
Why do you think it's not good?

277
00:20:00,030 --> 00:20:01,310
If you don't ask now, when will you ask?

278
00:20:01,310 --> 00:20:01,790
Ask him!

279
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:02,640
Exactly.

280
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:21,550
[Zhou Xiangxiang]

281
